{
  "_schema": [
    "The menu's content. Tabs hold items: {\"group\": \"Title\"} is a heading, {\"name\", \"sub\", \"show\", \"controls\"} is an entry.",
    "A control: id (unique, what expressions call it), key (the game's config key it drives), label, tag, type",
    "(choice | toggle | slider | action), options, min/max/step, div/decimals/suffix (slider text), default, help,",
    "show / disabled (expressions), disabledTag (a note while greyed out), dev (hidden unless dev mode is on: true / \"all\", or \"switch\" / \"pc\" for that platform only), restart.",
    "The PC shows every setting (the machines differ); a setting of the Switch is tuned once, becomes its default and is marked dev: \"switch\".",
    "Texts are English source text, translated at draw time by a table (English -> language). Logic never reads a",
    "text: an option is {\"id\": \"enhanced\", \"label\": \"Enhanced\"} (a bare string is both) and expressions, defaults and",
    "help compare ids. default: a value, an option id, or {\"switch\": v, \"pc\": v}. help: a text, or {option id: text}",
    "(toggles: \"1\" / \"0\").",
    "Expressions: ids, 'strings', numbers, == != && || ! and parentheses; names are the control ids plus \"platform\"",
    "('switch' | 'pc'), \"console\" (1 = no keyboard/mouse: the Switch, or a handheld run with GE_CONSOLE=1), \"handheld\" (1 = a small screen off the Switch: GE_HANDHELD=1; always 0 on the Switch) and \"dev\". A label can be {\"switch\": a, \"pc\": b}. Edit this file and press F5 in tools_pc/menuview to see the change."
  ],
  "tabs": [
    { "name": "Video", "items": [
      { "group": "Picture" },
      { "name": "Display", "controls": [
        { "id": "dispMode", "key": "__DisplayMode", "label": "Display mode", "type": "choice", "default": "enhanced",
          "options": [ { "id": "enhanced", "label": "Enhanced" }, { "id": "original", "label": "Original" }, { "id": "custom", "label": "Custom", "show": "platform == 'pc' || dev" } ],
          "help": { "enhanced": "The port's picture.", "original": "The N64 look.", "custom": "Shows every graphics option." } },
        { "id": "fullscreen", "key": "Video.Fullscreen", "label": "Fullscreen", "type": "toggle", "show": "console == 0" },
        { "id": "fsMode", "key": "Video.FullscreenMode", "label": "Fullscreen mode", "type": "choice",
          "show": "console == 0 && fullscreen == 1",
          "options": [ { "id": "borderless", "label": "Borderless" }, { "id": "exclusive", "label": "Exclusive" } ],
          "help": {"borderless": "A borderless window covering the screen.", "exclusive": "Takes the display for the game alone."} },
        { "id": "res", "key": "__Resolution", "label": "Resolution", "type": "select", "default": "r1080", "disabledTag": "(fullscreen)",
          "show": "console == 0", "disabled": "fullscreen == 1",
          "options": [ { "id": "r720", "label": "1280 x 720" }, { "id": "r900", "label": "1600 x 900" }, { "id": "r1080", "label": "1920 x 1080" }, { "id": "r1440", "label": "2560 x 1440" } ] },
        { "id": "aspect", "key": "Video.AspectMode", "label": "Aspect ratio", "type": "select",
          "options": [ { "id": "auto", "label": "Auto", "value": 0, "show": "dispMode != 'original'" }, { "id": "fit", "label": "Fit", "value": 4 }, { "id": "4x3", "label": "4:3", "value": 1 }, { "id": "16x9", "label": "16:9", "value": 2 }, { "id": "21x9", "label": "21:9", "value": 3, "show": "dispMode != 'original'" } ],
          "help": {"auto": "The picture takes the shape of the window, whatever it is: nothing is stretched, a wider window shows more of the sides.", "fit": "Picks the closest of 4:3, 16:9 and 21:9 to the window and adds bars around it.", "4x3": "Forces 4:3, with bars around it.", "16x9": "Forces 16:9, with bars around it.", "21x9": "Forces 21:9, with bars around it."}},
        { "id": "fov", "key": "Video.FovScale", "label": "Vertical field of view", "type": "slider", "min": 30, "max": 90, "step": 5, "per": 1.66666666666667, "suffix": " deg", "readout": "hfov",
          "help": "The vertical view angle: 60 is the original. The horizontal angle, shown beside it, follows the window's aspect ratio." },
        { "id": "split", "key": "Game.SplitScreen", "label": "Split screen", "type": "choice",
          "options": [ { "id": "horizontal", "label": "One above the other", "value": 0 }, { "id": "vertical", "label": "Side by side", "value": 1 } ],
          "help": { "horizontal": "Two players share the screen top and bottom, as in the original.", "vertical": "Two players share the screen left and right." } },
        { "id": "visuals", "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.Visuals", "label": "Visuals", "type": "choice",
          "options": [ { "id": "original", "label": "Original" }, { "id": "fixed", "label": "Fixed" }, { "id": "enhanced", "label": "Enhanced" } ],
          "help": {"original": "The console picture, with its flaws.", "fixed": "The original game's display flaws corrected.", "enhanced": "Fixed, plus a richer sky, scenery and effects."}},
        { "id": "crop", "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.SafeAreaCrop", "label": "Crop overscan", "type": "toggle", "dev": "switch"},
        { "id": "reset_display", "key": "__ResetEntry", "label": "Reset to defaults", "type": "action" }
      ] },
      { "name": "Asset packs", "controls": [
        { "id": "packs", "type": "packlist",
          "help": "Replacement textures and other assets: the .passets files in the assetpacks folder next to the game. Tick a pack to use it. The ticked packs are numbered: where two have the same texture, the lower number wins. The arrows change the order. The mod's own assets always win. Nothing changes until you choose Apply." }
      ] },
      { "name": "Performance", "show": "platform == 'pc' || dev", "controls": [
        { "id": "msaaHandheld", "key": "Video.MSAAHandheld", "label": "Anti-aliasing (handheld)", "type": "slider", "dev": "switch",
          "show": "dispMode == 'custom' && (platform == 'switch')", "options": [ { "id": "Off", "value": 1 }, { "id": "2x", "value": 2 }, { "id": "4x", "value": 4 } ],
          "help": {"Off": "Jagged edges. The fastest.", "2x": "Smoother edges, a little slower.", "4x": "The smoothest edges, the slowest."}},
        { "id": "msaaDocked", "key": "Video.MSAA", "label": "Anti-aliasing (docked)", "type": "slider", "dev": "switch",
          "show": "dispMode == 'custom' && (platform == 'switch')", "options": [ { "id": "Off", "value": 1 }, { "id": "2x", "value": 2 }, { "id": "4x", "value": 4 } ],
          "help": {"Off": "Jagged edges. The fastest.", "2x": "Smoother edges, a little slower.", "4x": "The smoothest edges, the slowest."}},
        { "id": "msaaPc", "key": "Video.MSAA", "label": "Anti-aliasing", "type": "slider", "restart": true,
          "show": "platform == 'pc'", "options": [ { "id": "Off", "value": 1 }, { "id": "2x", "value": 2 }, { "id": "4x", "value": 4 } ],
          "help": {"Off": "Jagged edges. The fastest.", "2x": "Smoother edges, a little slower.", "4x": "The smoothest edges, the slowest."}},
        { "id": "fxaa", "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.FXAA", "label": "FXAA", "type": "toggle", "dev": "switch",
          "help": "A final pass that smooths edges without blurring flat textures." },
        { "id": "vsync", "key": "Video.VSync", "label": "VSync", "type": "toggle", "dev": "switch"},
        { "id": "fps", "key": "Video.FpsCap", "label": "Frame rate cap", "type": "select", "dev": "switch",
          "options": [ { "id": "30", "value": 30 }, { "id": "60", "value": 60 }, { "id": "90", "value": 90 }, { "id": "120", "value": 120 }, { "id": "144", "value": 144 }, { "id": "165", "value": 165 }, { "id": "240", "value": 240 }, { "id": "auto", "label": "Auto", "value": -1 } ],
          "help": {"30": "Caps the game at 30 frames per second.", "60": "Caps the game at 60 frames per second.", "90": "Caps at 90. Adds blended in-between frames; the game still runs at 60.", "120": "Caps at 120. Adds blended in-between frames; the game still runs at 60.", "144": "Caps at 144. Adds blended in-between frames; the game still runs at 60.", "165": "Caps at 165. Adds blended in-between frames; the game still runs at 60.", "240": "Caps at 240. Adds blended in-between frames; the game still runs at 60.", "auto": "Matches your display. Above 60 adds blended in-between frames. The game still runs at 60."}},
        { "id": "showfps", "key": "Video.DisplayFPS", "label": "Show FPS", "type": "toggle", "dev": "switch"},
        { "id": "tex", "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.TextureFilter", "label": "Texture filter", "type": "choice", "dev": "switch",
          "options": [ { "id": "nearest", "label": "Nearest", "value": 0 }, { "id": "3point", "label": "3-point (N64)", "value": 2 }, { "id": "bilinear", "label": "Bilinear", "value": 1 }, { "id": "trilinear", "label": "Trilinear", "value": 3 } ],
          "help": {"nearest": "Hard-edged texels, no smoothing.", "3point": "The N64's own filter: it blends three texels, so edges look slightly angular. Includes mipmaps. Authentic, less smooth than bilinear.", "bilinear": "Blends four texels: smoother than the N64's own filter. No mipmaps.", "trilinear": "Bilinear plus generated mipmaps (smaller copies of each texture) blended together: distant textures shimmer less."}},
        { "id": "aniso", "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.Anisotropy", "label": "Anisotropic filtering", "type": "slider", "dev": "switch", "min": 1, "max": 16, "step": 1, "suffix": "x" },
        { "id": "draw", "per": 100, "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.DrawDistance", "label": "Draw distance", "type": "slider", "min": 100, "max": 800, "step": 25, "div": 100, "decimals": 1, "suffix": "x" },
        { "id": "fog", "per": 100, "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.FogDistance", "label": "Fog distance", "type": "slider", "min": 100, "max": 800, "step": 25, "div": 100, "decimals": 1, "suffix": "x" },
        { "id": "lod", "per": 100, "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.LodDistance", "label": "LOD distance", "type": "slider", "min": 100, "max": 800, "step": 25, "div": 100, "decimals": 1, "suffix": "x" },
        { "id": "fog_px", "show": "dispMode == 'custom'", "key": "Video.PerPixelFog", "label": "Per-pixel fog", "type": "toggle", "dev": "switch",
          "help": {"1": "The fog of every pixel comes from its own distance: exact.", "0": "The N64 way: the fog is worked out at the corners of each triangle and blended across it."} },
        { "id": "sky", "key": "Video.SkyScale", "label": "Sky and sea detail", "type": "choice", "dev": "switch",
          "show": "platform == 'pc' && visuals == 'enhanced'",
          "options": [ { "id": "full", "label": "Full" }, { "id": "half", "label": "Half (faster)" }, { "id": "quarter", "label": "Quarter (fastest)" } ],
          "help": { "half": "How sharp the Enhanced sky and sea are. Half draws them at a quarter of the pixels: faster, softer.",
                    "quarter": "How sharp the Enhanced sky and sea are. Quarter draws them at a sixteenth of the pixels: fastest, softest." } },
        { "id": "renderer", "key": "Video.Renderer", "label": "Renderer", "type": "choice", "default": "vulkan", "restart": true, "show": "platform == 'pc'",
          "options": [ { "id": "opengl", "label": "OpenGL" }, { "id": "vulkan", "label": "Vulkan" } ],
          "help": {"vulkan": "The default.", "opengl": "The fallback if Vulkan misbehaves on your GPU."}},
        { "id": "reset_performance", "key": "__ResetEntry", "label": "Reset to defaults", "type": "action" }
      ] },
      { "name": "Effects", "controls": [
